        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, a roof typically lasts 15 to 30 years\nfor standard asphalt shingles, while metal or tile systems can last 40 to 70+ years. High-elevation weather, intense UV rays, and heavy winter snowpacks heavily influence these numbers.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "15 to 30 years for standard asphalt shingles, while metal or tile systems can last 40 to 70+ years"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
